.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt VSDBUTIL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vsdbutil
.Nd set whether a volume uses file ownership
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a Ar path
.Op Fl c Ar path
.Op Fl d Ar path
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl x Ar path
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
records in a database, by volume UUID, whether each volume uses file ownership.
The options are done in the order given.
.Fl a ,
.Fl d ,
.Fl i
and
.Fl x
also update the mount with
.Xr mount 8 .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl a Ar path
Use ownership on the volume that holds
.Ar path .
.It Fl c Ar path
Show whether the volume that holds
.Ar path
uses ownership.
.It Fl d Ar path
Ignore ownership on the volume that holds
.Ar path .
The mounts of
.Pa /
and
.Pa /System/Volumes/Data
are left as they are.
.It Fl i
Use ownership on every mounted HFS or APFS volume.
.It Fl x Ar path
Remove the volume that holds
.Ar path
from the database.
.It Fl h
Show the usage.
.El
.Pp
Only root may use
.Fl a ,
.Fl d ,
.Fl i
and
.Fl x .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa /var/db/volinfo.database
The database.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8
